[21 CFR 117.126] Food safety plan.
(a) (a) Requirement for a food safety plan.
(a)(1) (1) You must prepare, or have prepared, and implement a written food safety plan.
(a)(2) (2) The food safety plan must be prepared, or its preparation overseen, by one or more preventive controls qualified individuals.
(b) (b) Contents of a food safety plan. The written food safety plan must include:
(b)(1) (1) The written hazard analysis as required by § 117.130(a)(2);
(b)(2) (2) The written preventive controls as required by § 117.135(b);
(b)(3) (3) The written supply-chain program as required by subpart G of this part;
(b)(4) (4) The written recall plan as required by § 117.139(a); and
(b)(5) (5) The written procedures for monitoring the implementation of the preventive controls as required by § 117.145(a);
(b)(6) (6) The written corrective action procedures as required by § 117.150(a)(1); and
(b)(7) (7) The written verification procedures as required by § 117.165(b).
(c) (c) Records. The food safety plan required by this section is a record that is subject to the requirements of subpart F of this part.

ideal_answer:
You must prepare, or have prepared, and implement a written food safety plan, and its preparation must be done or overseen by one or more preventive controls qualified individuals (21 CFR 117.126(a)(1) and (a)(2)).

The written food safety plan must include seven items (117.126(b)):
1. the written hazard analysis required by 117.130(a)(2);
2. the written preventive controls required by 117.135(b);
3. the written supply-chain program required by subpart G of this part;
4. the written recall plan required by 117.139(a);
5. the written procedures for monitoring implementation of the preventive controls required by 117.145(a);
6. the written corrective action procedures required by 117.150(a)(1); and
7. the written verification procedures required by 117.165(b).

The food safety plan is itself a record subject to the recordkeeping requirements of subpart F of this part (117.126(c)).

