- the justification for not reporting the action to FDA, which must contain conclusions and any follow-ups and be reviewed and evaluated by a designated person (b)(4)); and
- a copy of all communications regarding the correction or removal (b)(5)).

Retention. Records required under this section must be retained for 2 years beyond the expected life of the device, even if the manufacturer or importer has ceased to manufacture or import it (806.20(c)).

The justification requirement in 806.20(b)(4) is the point of the distinction: an exempt action is not an unrecorded action, and the decision not to report must itself be documented, reasoned and reviewed.

