ideal_answer:
21 CFR 820.198 is no longer in force - there are no live rows for it, and the former Subparts C through O of Part 820, which contained it, are [Reserved]. So there is no complaint file content specified at 820.198 today.

Complaint record content is now specified at 820.35(a). In addition to Clause 8.2.2 in ISO 13485, Complaint Handling (incorporated by reference at 820.7), the manufacturer must maintain records of the review, evaluation and investigation of any complaint involving the possible failure of a device, labeling or packaging to meet any of its specifications, and must include:
1. the name of the device (820.35(a)(1));
2. the date the complaint was received (820.35(a)(2));
3. any unique device identifier (UDI) or universal product code (UPC), and any other device identification(s) (820.35(a)(3));
4. the name, address and phone number of the complainant (820.35(a)(4));
5. the nature and details of the complaint (820.35(a)(5));
6. any correction or corrective action taken (820.35(a)(6)); and
7. any reply to the complainant (820.35(a)(7)).

So the route is 820.35(a) together with ISO 13485 Clause 8.2.2, not 820.198.

